From fcfda90d2ec8ec2c7fcc43b17f3a09cf9afb34db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:23:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add RWKU reworded-trained-probe evaluation and held-out
 answer-overlap audit

The paper's Gen columns measure two different things. MCF paraphrases, zsRE
rephrases and MQuAKE AtomicGen (the natural-language question of the same
atomic rewrite; training uses the cloze prompt) are unseen wordings of the
trained associations. RWKU's Gen is held-out probes about other facts of the
same person: a same-entity scope axis. This adds the like-for-like RWKU
column and an audit of how disjoint the held-out facts really are.

build_rwku_same50_paraphrases.py
  Rewords the 50 trained RWKU probes. The same-50 are 8 Level-1 cloze and 2
  Level-2 questions per person, and paraphrase_query only rewrites questions:
  on a cloze sentence it wraps the original verbatim, which would leave 40 of
  50 probes unchanged. Level-2 therefore uses paraphrase_query exactly as the
  official held-out paraphrases do; Level-1 is rewritten by a local
  open-weights model (probe_set_backends.LocalBackend, greedy, refuses the
  evaluated model). Candidates must differ from the original, keep a subject
  surface V2 accepts, keep exactly one blank (restored to the original blank
  string), and not contain the answer; rejects are kept with reasons. Output
  is frozen JSON with a sha256 sidecar and paraphrase_of_source_record_sha256
  for mapping back to trained rows.

evaluate_rwku_router_decomposition.py
  --same50-paraphrases adds a same50_paraphrase group with ground-truth rows;
  genie_exact and routing attribution now cover it, and the decomposition
  reports its base/V2/genie recovery, correct-route fraction and the
  rewording gap. Held-out groups are stratified by whether their answer
  matches a trained answer of the same person (exact, or whole-word
  containment of >= 3 characters): RWKU's split enforces exact-content
  disjointness, not fact disjointness, so a held-out question can ask for the
  same fact as a trained cloze probe. --analyze-rows computes that split from
  an existing rows file on CPU with no model. --run-dir is now optional only
  in that mode.

Tested on synthetic inputs: matcher cases (exact, contained, and a
substring that is not a whole word), the CPU analyzer end to end, and every
validator rejection path.

